<title>NEW ZEALAND: TranAlta Energy to lift stake in NZ arm.</title>
<headline>TranAlta Energy to lift stake in NZ arm.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>TransAlta New Zealand Ltd said on Tuesday it had bought the stakes in two New Zealand power stations owned by its majority owner, TransAlta Energy of Canada, in exchange for 25.2 million shares to be issued at NZ$1.75/share.</p>
<p>That would lift TransAlta Energy's stake in TransAlta NZ to 66 percent from 63 percent, the company said in a statement.</p>
